  "acceptance": [
    "Approved synthetic skill text I know Linux but have no Kubernetes experience previously scored 100 for those two skills. It now scores 50 with Linux supported and Kubernetes withheld from positive evidence.",
    "Baseline skill coverage and optional experience weighting share bounded positive-evidence extraction. Supported English denials, aspirations, unknown wording and approved contradictions do not become positive skill claims.",
    "Only approved, verified, source-backed facts with finite numeric confidence from 80 through 100 are eligible. NaN, infinity, booleans, strings, missing values and out-of-range confidence do not supply skill/experience evidence.",
    "Supported contradictions retain NO_APPROVED_EVIDENCE plus a review reason rather than inferring lack of qualification. Unapproved negative text cannot invalidate approved facts; positive no-downtime/not-only controls retain credit.",
    "Real fixture recalculation, job list and explanation API persist 50/100 skill-plus-experience scores for positive Linux and negative Active Directory evidence. SQLite reopening preserves exact explanations. Explicit fact correction creates a new profile version and permits 100 after recalculation.",
    "Matching does not edit facts or approval flags. Added evidence reasons and explanations do not echo raw private fixture fact text.",
    "Unit-contract repairs preserve existing assertions: project/port Compose contract and fixture isolation are checked, invalid targets never reach the runner, current heatmap evidence fields are asserted, and an imported production probe is no longer miscollected as a pytest test.",
    "All three initial broad-suite failures reproduced on a pristine git archive of f399e00 before repair. No production credential, Compose or heatmap implementation was changed by the test repairs."
